! ========================================================================
! 8 | ITEM-LEVEL RESPONSE-SET FACTOR
! The syntax fixes all loadings in the declared Mplus variable range to 1.
! The variable range follows USEVARIABLES order (not lexical item order).
! This models a uniform response tendency across selected indicators.
! The wide range should be checked against item coding and intended set.
! ========================================================================
  RSET by MQ34_2-MQ73_5@1; 





! ========================================================================
! 9 | REQUESTED OUTPUT
! STDYX provides standardized estimates; MOD(40) requests modification
! indices meeting the specified 40 threshold in the output.
! Do not equate absence of MI >= 40 with global model confirmation.
! Use fit, parsimony, residual pattern, and independent replication.
! ========================================================================
OUTPUT: STDYX MOD(40);
  

 
 
    








